The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError

The fix was simple: change `parts[1]` to `parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split array.
